<title>THAILAND: Thai bourse delays stricter forced sale rules.</title>
<headline>Thai bourse delays stricter forced sale rules.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Stock Exchange of Thailand (SET) on Thursday reacted to heavy falls in Thai stocks this month by announcing a six-month delay in adopting stricter rules that force indebted investors to sell stocks to help them meet margin calls.</p>
<p>SET president Singh Tangtatswas told reporters the bourse decided to postpone a January 1 deadline for enforcing the market's maintenance margin rules to July 1, 1997.</p>
</text>
